#: ../../../cards.md:461
msgid ""
"Migrate, then flip the flag While the legacy separators are enabled (the "
"default), the raw-line scan runs on **every** card, so a stray column-0 "
"`^^^` or `+++` — even inside a code block, and even in a card that has "
"already migrated to the `card-header` / `card-footer` directives — is still "
"treated as a separator (mis-splitting the card and emitting a mixed-syntax "
"warning). The single-parse robustness is only realized once the separators "
"are turned off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cards.md:469
msgid ""
"The recommended order is therefore **migrate first, then flip the flag**: "
"convert every card to the directives, then set `sd_card_legacy_separators = "
"False` in your `conf.py`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cards.md:474
msgid ""
"With `sd_card_legacy_separators = False`, `^^^` / `+++` lines are no longer "
"scanned — but they do **not** reliably render as literal text, so migrate "
"before flipping:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cards.md:478
msgid "in MyST, a bare `+++` line is a block break and silently disappears;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cards.md:479
msgid ""
"in reStructuredText, a `^^^` / `++++` line can raise a docutils `CRITICAL` "
"\"Unexpected section title or transition\" error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cards.md:482
msgid ""
"Builds that treat warnings as errors The deprecation warning is **on by "
"default**, so a build run with `-W` (or `--fail-on-warning`) fails while any "
"document still uses `^^^` / `+++`. There are two remedies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cards.md:487
msgid ""
"migrate those cards to the `card-header` / `card-footer` directives (above); "
"or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cards.md:488
msgid ""
"keep the legacy syntax for now and silence the warning in your `conf.py`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cards.md:490
msgid "suppress_warnings = [\"design.card_legacy\"]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cards.md:495
msgid ""
"**Timeline**: deprecated now (default on) → default off at `1.0` → removed "
"at `2.0`."
msgstr ""
